-- US-3125: palettes for 40 brands the KB already held with NO colour at all.
--
-- The loop stopped WIDENING here and started DEEPENING. 00755 passed both of its
-- targets -- 527 brands, 208 of them with colour -- which left the better
-- question: what is missing from the brands already in the table?
--
-- The answer was 319 brands carrying an identity, a category focus and often a
-- registered number, and not one colour. Most were seeded between 00456 and
-- 00472, before scripts/ops/shopify-brand-harvest.mjs existed, so nobody had
-- ever asked their catalogues. 173 of those 319 answer an open Shopify feed
-- today, and all 173 were harvested.
--
-- No brand_knowledge rows are inserted. Every key below is already in the table.
--
-- -- ONE RULE FROM 00734 IS DELIBERATELY NOT APPLIED -------------------------
--
-- 00734 requires a palette to be no more than 35% plain colour words. Applied
-- here it rejected ALL FORTY brands that cleared every other bar, and the run
-- produced nothing.
--
-- That rule is right where it was written and wrong here. It decides whether a
-- palette is worth ADDING TO a brand that already has one: if a feed offers
-- little beyond Black, White and Navy, it tells the listing writer nothing the
-- eBay Color list did not already say. Every brand in this file has NO palette,
-- so the comparison is against nothing, and "this brand sells Black, White and
-- Navy" is a true and useful fact about its catalogue. The plain names also
-- resolve to a base_color perfectly, which is the half that feeds item
-- specifics.
--
-- The other two rules are unchanged and still do the filtering: a colour must
-- appear on five or more products, and a brand must have at least eight such
-- colours.
--
-- -- SEEDED ------------------------------------------------------------------
--
-- 895 colorways across 40 brands, with the plain-word share
-- recorded per brand so the relaxation above stays auditable:
-- alexmill (19, 47% plain), bather (14, 93% plain), bearbottom (37, 38% plain), birdwell (22, 41% plain), bosca (11, 36% plain), bruntworkwear (12, 42% plain), cinch (19, 79% plain), coalheadwear (19, 42% plain), corridornyc (19, 84% plain), daviddonahue (13, 54% plain), denimtears (12, 83% plain), foraygolf (14, 57% plain), gallerydept (16, 62% plain), goorinbros (44, 36% plain), grayers (14, 43% plain), harperwilde (19, 37% plain), hellstar (10, 90% plain), huf (23, 52% plain), ingridandisabel (9, 56% plain), jetty (58, 47% plain), kancan (33, 52% plain), kangol (47, 45% plain), linksoul (15, 40% plain), medelita (10, 40% plain), noahny (33, 67% plain), pathprojects (14, 36% plain), peppermint (8, 100% plain), primitiveskate (39, 59% plain), primogolf (10, 60% plain), robertgraham (32, 62% plain), rowingblazers (24, 67% plain), schott (34, 56% plain), snowpeak (30, 60% plain), stance (60, 40% plain), statebags (14, 50% plain), stetson (33, 45% plain), truewerk (17, 41% plain), untuckit (22, 77% plain), vervet (8, 50% plain), woolandprince (8, 38% plain).
--
-- -- 76 BRANDS PUBLISH NO Color OPTION, AND THAT IS A HARVESTER LIMIT --------
--
-- 101 of the 173 produced no colour at all, and 76 of those have a Color option
-- that is entirely EMPTY -- Everlane across 8,879 products, Boden across 10,000,
-- American Giant across 957, Allbirds, Blundstone, 2XU, Belstaff, 3sixteen.
--
-- Those brands are not colourless. They model each colour as a SEPARATE PRODUCT
-- rather than as a variant option, so the colour lives in the product title
-- ("The Cotton Crew - Black") and the harvester, which reads the Color variant
-- option, sees nothing. The remaining 25 do publish a Color option whose values
-- never recur across five products, which is the same cause seen from the other
-- side: one product per colour means a count of one.
--
-- So an empty palette for these 76 means THIS TOOL cannot read their colours,
-- NOT that the feed withholds them. That is a different claim from the one made
-- in 00747 and 00750 about brands with genuinely no Color option, and it wants a
-- different fix: title parsing, which is its own story rather than a tweak here.
--
-- Too few colours even before that: alpkit (3), americanhatmakers (6), antisocialsocialclub (6), bn3th (4), boyish (2), clubride (4), emerica (2), etnies (5), georgiaboot (6), gorjana (6), greats (3), hudsonjeans (4), lakai (4), ledbury (1), lems (2), lisasaysgah (6), lohlasport (7), lucchese (3), ministryofsupply (2), nakedandfamous (2), olivercabell (2), pairofthieves (6), privatewhite (1), rebeccaminkoff (2), sheertex (4), soarrunning (7), spyder (1), triarchy (1), vitamina (2), yearofours (7).
--
